  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Second Rwanda Urban Development Project (RUDP II) 2023-2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall development objective of RUDP II is to improve access to basic services, enhance resilience and strengthen integrated urban planning and management. Denmark is co-funding the project&apos;s sub-component 1b. The objective for sub-component 1b is wetland rehabilitation and flood risk reduction.

The sub-component 1b will support the design, implementation and monitoring of nature-based solutions to reduce flood risks, enhance biodiversity, and strengthen resilience in the City of Kigali, Rwanda. This allows for subsequent scalability within a Secondary Cities programme, by adding a further wetlands component, once scoping and feasibility studies are completed.

The project if anticipating the following results; 1) People benefitting from flood risk reduction and wetland rehabilitation interventions in Kigali (220,500 persons), 2) Rehabilitation of wetlands (491 Ha), 3) Development of long-term management strategy and business plan for management and maintenance of rehabilitated wetlands, and 4) Development and operationalization of greenhouse gas accounting and reporting framework</narrative>
  </description>
